Id: init010e
Severity: ERROR
Category: tigris
Check: tiger tigris

Tiger is running as root but the directory holding its check scripts is
owned by another user. Tiger never runs a check script owned by someone
other than the user running it (see misc024e), so every check would be
skipped and the report would be empty. A tree owned by the person who
ran sudo is the exception: no privilege boundary is crossed, so it runs.
Otherwise make the tree root's, for example with 'chown -R root:root' on
the Tiger directory, or run it from an installed copy.
